NEW-CITAWIKI: BASIC RECOVERY AND STOPPING COMMANDS
=================================================

Configuration directory:
/k8s/configs/new-citawiki

Kubernetes namespace:
cita-wiki

Production public IP:
142.1.127.104

New test deployment public IP:
142.1.127.107


1. RESTART THE WEB APPLICATION
------------------------------

Restart the web Deployment without deleting the Deployment or its Service:

kubectl -n cita-wiki rollout restart deployment/new-citawiki

kubectl -n cita-wiki rollout status deployment/new-citawiki --timeout=300s

To restart the database Deployment instead:

kubectl -n cita-wiki rollout restart deployment/new-citawiki-db

kubectl -n cita-wiki rollout status deployment/new-citawiki-db --timeout=300s


2. TAKE THE TEST SITE OFFLINE TEMPORARILY
-----------------------------------------

Delete only the new web LoadBalancer Service. The web and database
Deployments keep running, but public access through 142.1.127.107 stops.

kubectl -n cita-wiki delete service new-citawiki

Restore the Service later:

kubectl apply -f /k8s/configs/new-citawiki/web-service.yaml

Check the Service:

kubectl -n cita-wiki get service new-citawiki

The Service requests IP 142.1.127.107. MetalLB must still have that
address available for it to be assigned again.


3. RECREATE A DELETED DEPLOYMENT
--------------------------------

If only the web Deployment was deleted, recreate it:

kubectl apply -f /k8s/configs/new-citawiki/web-deployment.yaml

kubectl -n cita-wiki rollout status deployment/new-citawiki --timeout=300s

If only the database Deployment was deleted, recreate it:

kubectl apply -f /k8s/configs/new-citawiki/db-deployment.yaml

kubectl -n cita-wiki rollout status deployment/new-citawiki-db --timeout=300s

The existing PVCs and referenced Secrets must still exist. The database
Deployment must reconnect to the existing new-citawiki-db-pvc.

Check the resources after recovery:

kubectl -n cita-wiki get deployment,service,pods,pvc

If both Deployments or their Services need to be restored, apply the
Kustomize configuration:

cd /k8s/configs/new-citawiki

kubectl apply -k .

This Kustomize configuration includes the web Deployment and Service,
and the database Deployment and Service. It excludes both PVC manifests.


4. PERMANENTLY REMOVE THE TEST WEB APPLICATION
----------------------------------------------

Only do this when intentionally removing the new web application and its
public Service. This does not delete the database Deployment, database
Service, PVCs, ConfigMaps, or Secrets.

kubectl -n cita-wiki delete deployment new-citawiki

kubectl -n cita-wiki delete service new-citawiki

To recreate the web application later:

kubectl apply -f /k8s/configs/new-citawiki/web-deployment.yaml

kubectl apply -f /k8s/configs/new-citawiki/web-service.yaml

Verify recovery:

kubectl -n cita-wiki rollout status deployment/new-citawiki --timeout=300s

kubectl -n cita-wiki get deployment,service,pods


IMPORTANT DATA-PROTECTION NOTES
===============================

1. Do not delete new-citawiki-files-pvc or new-citawiki-db-pvc during
   routine restarts, updates, or Deployment recovery.

2. The PVCs contain persistent wiki files and database data. A PVC
   manifest describes a storage request; it is not a backup of the data.
   Recreating a deleted PVC may provision an empty volume.

3. Keep verified SQL dumps and backups of the underlying wiki files
   separately from the Kubernetes manifests.

4. Do not delete or modify the production cita-wiki Deployment,
   production Service, or production PVCs when working on new-citawiki.

5. Production uses public IP 142.1.127.104. The new test deployment
   uses public IP 142.1.127.107.

6. Before applying saved manifests, verify that required ConfigMaps and
   Secrets still exist. Review configuration changes before applying them.

7. The database image in db-deployment.yaml is:
   docker.io/citadockerhub/mariadb:11.4.13-ubu2404-cita1

8. The database Deployment references the Secret new-citawiki-db-secret,
   key root_password. The web Deployment references the application
   Secret new-citawiki-app-secret, key password.

9. A successful Kubernetes rollout does not by itself prove that the
   wiki works correctly. Check pod status, database connectivity, Apache
   configuration, and wiki page responses after recovery.

10. Deleting a Deployment does not normally delete its PVCs, but deleting
    a PVC may endanger access to the persistent data. Never delete the
    PVCs as a routine troubleshooting step.
